+
+                // Cost of removing city from position i:
+                // Remove edges: (i-1)->city at step i, city->next at step i+1
+                // Add edge: (i-1)->next at step i (but step indices shift!)
+
+                // This is complex with penalties. Let's compute delta directly.
+                // When we remove city at position i and insert after position j:
+                // If j < i: positions j+1..i-1 shift right by 1, city goes to j+1
+                // If j > i: positions i+1..j shift left by 1, city goes to j
+
+                // For small N or to keep things fast, let's compute affected edges' cost change
+                // Actually, with penalty positions shifting, this is non-trivial.
+                // Let's use a simpler approach: just compute the cost difference for affected edges.
+
+                // Simpler: do an Or-opt by removing tour[i] and inserting after tour[j]
+                // Build new tour segment and compute cost difference
+
+                // For speed, let's just do the move and compute cost delta on a few edges
+                // But penalty positions make this tricky since all positions after the change shift.
+
+                // For very large N, we need O(1) delta. Let's approximate:
